      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think worlds have some control over this. I've been in some worlds where it feels like I can hop in a bleacher from the 3 point line of a basketball court. I would like this sensitivity to be tameable.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-21T15:37:42.202Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Relevant: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1137-lens-pickup-radius-interferes-with-camera-ui\n\nIn general the enormous radius for picking up most objects in worlds as well as vrc camera interferes with interacting with VRC UI (like camera controls) and overlays required to use my computer at the same time like XSOverlay or OVR toolkit. I grab or pickup something on accident more often then I do on purpose.\n\nGive the user to set a distance in which grab-able objects are grabbed. Both for things like the VRC Camera and in world objects using VRC_Pickup. \n\nAdditionally objects grabbed by laser at any distance should have configurable settings or an ability to be toggled. \n\nThis could go in comfort settings and it wont interfere with people who need the larger radius but will allow for people to take advantage of the sub-millimeter tracking modern controllers have  and interact with objects in a way that feels more dexterous instead of like we have magnets duct taped to our hands.",
